# Wayfinder wrote this file when it created this repository.
#
# It holds the two values the workflows cannot read from anywhere else: what
# this service is called, and which `wf` build CI installs. Everything else CI
# needs — the Wayfinder server, the service account each job signs in as, the
# environment it deploys to and the AWS region — is a GitHub variable Wayfinder
# set at the same time, and the per-environment ones are visible only to a job
# that declares that environment.

# Names the stack instances: <service>-pr<number> for a pull request,
# <service>-develop and <service>-prod for the two long-lived deployments. The
# two ECR repositories are <service>-message-service and <service>-frontend.
WF_SERVICE_NAME=${{ .Inputs.serviceName }}

# The `wf` CLI build CI installs. Empty tracks the latest development build;
# set it to a released version (e.g. v3.2.1) to pin.
WF_CLI_VERSION=

# There is no container registry here, and that is the point. The ECR registry
# is per account and is always there; `pushimages` creates this service's two
# repositories the first time anything deploys, and pushes to them as the
# deployment identity. So there is no registry address to record here and no
# registry credential to store. CI passes RELEASE and nothing else.
